Timing of interFoam, interIsoFoam, interIsoGoam (ddtCorr off) and fluxinator at max Co 0.1
on 95x20, 190x40 and 380x80, three repeats, to t = 6 s, without the wave gauge (made when the
gauge was interfaceHeight, which rebuilds a mesh search tree every step, about half of the step
time; the gauge is now surfacePosition, whose cost is negligible).
Set-ups: solvers_maxCo_ddtCorrOff 0006-0008 (95x20), 0018-0020 (190x40), 0030-0032 (380x80) and
finalSolver_maxCo 0008, 0020, 0032, with endTime 6 and functions.surfacePosition1.enabled false in
system/controlDict.run (makeCases.sh).
./runAll.sh: at most 8 concurrent unpinned runs, nothing else on the machine.
python3 analyse.py writes ../data/timing_maxCo0.1.csv (time per step over 2 <= t <= 6 s).
Part II Figure fig:selCost combines it with the step counts of the full 30 s runs.
Superseded, kept for the record: ../timing_maxCo0.1 (pinned with taskset, 30-40 % spread) and
../timing_maxCo0.1_t6 (unpinned, with the gauge, 12 runs at a time).
